"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"41f9e6e5b105b62888f123f33a7f569a85c5bd6bb494ff50be4e1e59ebe1df9d","event_uuid":"3367096b-4e34-4c07-b11e-0fca58848642","position":{"commit_sha":"2129409d1fd0ee4120f362dc78cf7f9493e51dbd","position":"1788618016123978001-3367096b-4e34-4c07-b11e-0fca58848642"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d06a76b14953a2a68c3094158890ab286c886d7e7588bc450a4113889d5cc856","event_uuid":"aeefd2ea-f888-4626-a283-a4810df240dc","position":{"commit_sha":"8070bf7252a34839e466035099fe689748a2c04e","position":"1788623462010111001-aeefd2ea-f888-4626-a283-a4810df240dc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788570529329591028,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"072e08bb-75ad-49b9-8e0d-5393935fd392","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ad92-dadf-b0fa-43da"},{"link_uuid":"01511ac2-3189-4a0b-ab34-f72d8db6af2a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"fdea-9745-e4de-4326"},{"link_uuid":"f35967e3-7650-4073-b4d8-a218ca5ebf7c","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c1e6-3b0d-c1da-4e59"},{"link_uuid":"6761f437-ffa9-44b8-a4e5-637995725d27","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"314e-07c6-57cc-40d5"},{"link_uuid":"af6f1db1-db64-4c81-b437-e14178de7dd5","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e8ae-ef90-bbe0-4d37"},{"link_uuid":"e68c5d26-3503-4ca2-a3ea-d1147b83bc10","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"36c8-489b-7df0-4cf0"},{"link_uuid":"87474865-b4d8-4407-9cc6-137a467a558b","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"f724-651f-1cab-43b0"},{"link_uuid":"263160b9-bdb1-4733-b13e-2fa987c9d381","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"62cf-bae4-68cb-4573"},{"link_uuid":"1c9e036b-0cdb-4f35-8218-62f939c22da0","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"4298-b694-a0f8-403d"},{"link_uuid":"eff363d2-9c99-4df2-8a5a-5e9980d88c97","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"d4b9-37a1-96e3-4edd"},{"link_uuid":"41d192be-80ea-4a03-958b-7ce34b9ad68a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c0d2-bcee-47c5-45f6"},{"link_uuid":"48cd53a8-f6b4-4f59-9fc9-0da259743bc5","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"427d-b94c-cbcd-445d"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nTwelve `infra/scripts` files contain audited repeated, historical, obvious, or stale prose. Scope was revalidated on `origin/main@d6669496cae4`; this includes the current unclamped `pct_of_cap` contract in `observability.sh`. Operational, security, and recovery contracts must remain explicit.\n\n## Approach\nCondense only anchored standalone comments and blank lines. Preserve every executable/configuration line byte-for-byte. Bind each policy directive to its following executable line and preserve both text and placement.\n\nUse a before/final Git comparison whose only ignored lines match `^([[:space:]]*#[^!].*|[[:space:]]*#[[:space:]]*|[[:space:]]*)$`; do not ignore semicolon or HTML-shaped lines. The anti-vacuity census is 12 shebangs, one SC2016 directive, two gitleaks allowances, one `mechanism-ok` marker, and no tickets-boundary/raw-git directives.\n\n## Scope\n- `autodeploy.sh` — header; marker/backoff/tunable declarations; contracts adjoining marker, bot health/disposition, log capture, Docker/disk-pressure helpers, and `mcp_*` helpers; orchestration sections through the component-marker footer. Retain independent markers/backoffs, no incomplete advancement, bounded resources/drain, secrets-before-start, candidate validation, exact nginx rollback, observability/certbot deployment, and distinct deploy/detect triggers.\n- `bootstrap-gerrit-admin.sh` — header, dev-login account creation, shard/ref construction, fetch-or-orphan body, and final restart. Retain pre-OAuth bootstrap, idempotent key installation, account checks, and public `ADMIN_PUBKEY`.\n- `compose-up.sh` — header; site/volume enumeration; four cap installers; site, scratch, plugin/hook, OAuth, materializer, and final compose-up blocks. The reaper removes only old, unprotected exited/dead containers; compose/MCP-labelled or named containers, grace-window containers, running containers, force removal, and volume removal remain outside its reach. Retain parent-only gate-scratch and nonfatal installer/materializer postures.\n- `config-check.sh` — header, YAML check, volume extractors/comparison, both negative self-tests, and real check. Retain daemon-independent validation and loud empty-enumeration failure.\n- `fetch-secrets.sh` — header mapping; required/optional readers and ordering; PAT fallback; authorship/op-cert files; static-token JSON; Jira degradation; generated env. Retain blank-key semantics, atomic permissioned writes, nonlogging, and gitleaks directives; do not call `MCP_HMAC_SIGNING_KEY` a current verdict signer.\n- `install-autodeploy.sh` and `install-certbot-timer.sh` — headers and numbered installation sections. Retain idempotence, mirror/bootstrap, disabled timer, host-nginx/dnf/venv fallbacks, HTTP-01 webroot, renewal/reload cadence, and arguments.\n- `materialize-mcp-upstream.sh` — header and numbered/only-if-absent/reload sections. Retain that nginx requires the installed include to supply at least one `server` line: the script checks the seed, copies only when the target is absent, and optionally reloads. Do not claim validation of an existing target or atomic replacement.\n- `materialize-opcert-guard.sh` — header and numbered/only-if-absent/reload sections. Retain raw guard handling, `umask 077`, unrelated env entries, atomic env replacement, direct nginx-map write, deny-all fallback, brief rotation 403, and the application header check.\n- `mcp-entrypoint.sh` — header/config; safe-clear helpers; inode-lock contract; tracker/code clone; ensure/provision path; provision-only/background/PID-1 footer. Retain asynchronous convergence, safe clearing, double-checks, blobless clone, URL-scoped credentials, PID-1 `exec`, and shellcheck directive.\n- `observability.sh` — metric catalog; numbered sections; bounded journal helpers; the comment bound to `pct_of_cap`; `docker_du_bytes`, `docker_ledger_bytes`, marker publishing, and final exit. Retain one `docker system df` format/census; SI/binary parsing; four-known-row total; unknown-row ignore; known-size parse failure; `-1` sentinels; percentage stripping; `read` rather than `set --`; and independent total, percentage, reclaimable, reaper, and quota publications. `pct_of_cap` must remain unclamped because budget metrics must expose values above 100 when a best-effort cap is exceeded; CloudWatch's `Percent` unit is a label, while byte gauges preserve magnitude. Retain bounded probes, MCP 401 health, publish-before-cursor, mirror failure `1`, intentional fail-safe values, and final exit `0`.\n- `reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh` — header, identity, deferred clone, embedded-Python epoch reconciliation, and ensure-registry. Retain durable setup, merge-as-union, guarded epoch adoption, and no moving-ref reset/discard.\n\nConsumers include systemd, deployment/config gates, nginx, containers, CloudWatch alarms, security checks, and operators. `compose-up.sh` is an autodeploy detect-only materializer path; `observability.sh` is reinstalled through `OBS_PATHS` and feeds container alarms. `container-cap.sh` is outside this parent cohort and is tracked separately.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only anchored standalone comments or blank lines change.\n- [ ] Executable and configuration lines remain byte-identical.\n- [ ] Every directive remains byte-identical and bound to the same following statement.\n- [ ] Each Scope constraint has a cited PASS row in the independent semantic matrix.\n- [ ] Each consumer contract has a cited PASS row in the independent semantic matrix.\n- [ ] Each edited block has a cited `bloat-removal=PASS` row and is shorter.\n- [ ] The content guard and focused non-live checks pass.\n- [ ] Path-scoped `git diff --check` passes.\n- [ ] Worktree-venv `make verify` passes.\n- [ ] Missing or failing matrix rows block closure.\n\n## Verification\nRun the corrected executable-line/directive guards, ShellCheck policy, config self-tests, focused autodeploy/MCP/observability/reviewbot suites, path-scoped diff check, and `make verify`. A non-author reviewer posts the leaf-linked matrix with immutable before/final citations; it is authoritative for prose quality.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/scripts/bootstrap-gerrit-admin.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/scripts/compose-up.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/scripts/config-check.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/scripts/install-autodeploy.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/scripts/install-certbot-timer.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/scripts/materialize-mcp-upstream.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/scripts/materialize-opcert-guard.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/scripts/observability.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","49ac-d7e5-f383-4d7f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"49ac-d7e5-f383-4d7f","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_id":"0165-f432-0580-4117","ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in infra/scripts","verify_commands":[{"command":"rtk git diff --exit-code --ignore-matching-lines='^\\([[:space:]]*#[^!].*\\|[[:space:]]*#[[:space:]]*\\|[[:space:]]*\\)$' HEAD^ HEAD -- infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh infra/scripts/bootstrap-gerrit-admin.sh infra/scripts/compose-up.sh infra/scripts/config-check.sh infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh infra/scripts/install-autodeploy.sh infra/scripts/install-certbot-timer.sh infra/scripts/materialize-mcp-upstream.sh infra/scripts/materialize-opcert-guard.sh infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh infra/scripts/observability.sh infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh","dd_id":"preserve-executable-lines","dd_text":"Only ordinary standalone comments or blank lines may differ."},{"command":"rtk proxy env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python -c 'import re, subprocess, sys\npat = re.compile(r\"^\\s*#\\s*(?:!|shellcheck\\b|gitleaks:|tickets-boundary-ok:|raw-git-ok:|mechanism-ok:|pragma:|noqa\\b|type:\\s*ignore\\b)\", re.I)\ndef pairs(ref, path):\n    lines = subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"show\", f\"{ref}:{path}\"], text=True).splitlines()\n    out = []\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\n        if not pat.search(line):\n            continue\n        nxt = next((candidate for candidate in lines[i + 1:] if candidate.strip() and not candidate.lstrip().startswith(\"#\")), \"<EOF>\")\n        out.append((line, nxt))\n    return out\nbad = [path for path in sys.argv[1:] if pairs(\"HEAD^\", path) != pairs(\"HEAD\", path)]\nassert not bad, f\"directive/shebang text or placement changed: {bad}\"' infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh infra/scripts/bootstrap-gerrit-admin.sh infra/scripts/compose-up.sh infra/scripts/config-check.sh infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh infra/scripts/install-autodeploy.sh infra/scripts/install-certbot-timer.sh infra/scripts/materialize-mcp-upstream.sh infra/scripts/materialize-opcert-guard.sh infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh infra/scripts/observability.sh infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh","dd_id":"preserve-shell-directives","dd_text":"Shebangs and policy directives retain exact text and next-statement placement."},{"command":"rtk proxy env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_shellcheck.py","dd_id":"shellcheck-contracts","dd_text":"Shell syntax and ShellCheck policy pass."},{"command":"rtk bash infra/scripts/config-check.sh","dd_id":"config-contracts","dd_text":"Infrastructure config and volume negative tests pass."},{"command":"rtk proxy env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest -q tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_*.py tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py tests/scripts/test_container_cap.py tests/scripts/test_docker_storage_cap.py tests/scripts/test_journald_cap.py tests/scripts/test_vartmp_cap.py tests/unit/test_check_deploy_manifest.py","dd_id":"autodeploy-contracts","dd_text":"Autodeploy and host-cap contracts pass."},{"command":"rtk proxy env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest -q tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py tests/scripts/test_mcp_client_pats.py tests/unit/test_rp04_s6_opcert_startup_heldout.py","dd_id":"mcp-opcert-contracts","dd_text":"MCP provisioning, secrets, and op-cert startup contracts pass."},{"command":"rtk proxy env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest -q tests/scripts/test_observability_*.py tests/unit/test_alarm_actions_terraform.py tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py tests/unit/test_marker_single_emission_f829.py","dd_id":"observability-contracts","dd_text":"Observability metrics, alarms, scratch, and markers pass."},{"command":"rtk proxy env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest -q tests/unit/test_reviewbot_ensure_tickets.py tests/scripts/test_reviewbot_entrypoint.py tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_reviewbot_ensure_path.py","dd_id":"reviewbot-store-contracts","dd_text":"Review-bot store convergence and entrypoint integration pass."},{"command":"rtk git diff --check HEAD^ HEAD -- infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh infra/scripts/bootstrap-gerrit-admin.sh infra/scripts/compose-up.sh infra/scripts/config-check.sh infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh infra/scripts/install-autodeploy.sh infra/scripts/install-certbot-timer.sh infra/scripts/materialize-mcp-upstream.sh infra/scripts/materialize-opcert-guard.sh infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh infra/scripts/observability.sh infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh","dd_id":"diff-integrity","dd_text":"Declared paths contain no whitespace errors."},{"command":"rtk proxy env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify","dd_id":"full","dd_text":"The repository verification gate passes."}]},"source_event_uuids":["76adbe9b-3be9-49ad-b8d7-ac278cf55ccd","57966a17-0bac-459c-a160-9c9bcf605881","90cd13a7-0eb2-42dc-91b4-162dac99e517","a289bb7d-50a5-4f3e-983c-c7c8cc1a18ea","f780dcac-ddcc-41dc-98cb-bdf29de0ef03","eb88b3e3-018c-48bc-a2bb-756b8ac41bd6","e421fe6